.TH tuuuid n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuuuid
.PP
UUID generation and inspection in pure Tcl. Supports version 4 (random) and version 7 (Unix\-time\-ordered, RFC 9562). Random bytes come from \fB/dev/urandom\fR when available, otherwise from \fBrand()\fR (non\-cryptographic fallback).
.SS API
.CS
set id  [::tclutils::tuuuid::generate]            ;# v4 by default
set id7 [::tclutils::tuuuid::generate -version 7] ;# time-ordered
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBgenerate ?\-version 4|7?\fR — a canonical UUID string (default 4).
.IP \(bu
\fBv4\fR — random version\-4 UUID.
.IP \(bu
\fBv7\fR — time\-ordered version\-7 UUID (sorts by creation time).
.IP \(bu
\fBnil\fR — the nil UUID \fB00000000\-0000\-0000\-0000\-000000000000\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBvalidate uuid\fR — 1 if \fBuuid\fR is a canonical UUID string, else 0.
.IP \(bu
\fBversion uuid\fR — the version digit (1..8); errors on an invalid UUID.
.PP
Errors: \fB{TCLUTILS TUUUID VERSION}\fR (bad \fB\-version\fR), \fB{TCLUTILS TUUUID INVALID}\fR (not a UUID).
